    "result_text": "The full test suite (the single `AcceptanceTest`) is green. Done.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe spec: on successful create, enqueue a welcome notification \u2014 emit via the logger named `NOTIFY` a line containing the owner id and the memberId.\n\n1. **New function class** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnqueueWelcomeNotification.java`. It reads the persisted `Owner` via `@Val` and logs to a logger named `NOTIFY`, including both `owner.getId()` and `owner.getMemberId()`. It mirrors the existing `AuditOwnerCreated` step's conventions.\n\n2. **Wired it into the pipeline** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`. Inserted a `welcome` step between `audit` and `respond`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbors. Placement is after `save` (so `id` and `memberId` are assigned) and only on the success path, so it fires only on a successful create.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` test passes: it captures the `NOTIFY` logger and asserts a line contains both the returned owner id and memberId \u2014 the emitted line is e.g. `welcome notification queued for owner id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`. `BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test run, 0 failures.",
